  "Question": "Bridget bought a bag of apples at the grocery store. She gave half of the apples to Ann. Then she gave Cassie \\(3\\) apples, keeping \\(4\\) apples for herself. How many apples did Bridget buy?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\)",
    "E": "\\(14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Just before giving Cassie her apples, Bridget had \\(3+4=7\\) apples. These were the half left after giving Ann the other half. The original bag therefore contained two equal groups of \\(7\\) apples:\n\\[\n2\\times7=14.\n\\]\nBridget bought \\(\\boxed{14}\\) apples, choice E.",
